Set the module-level settings: the domain published names live under,
which DNS provider hosts it, the credential olr uses to prove the domain
is yours, and who the certificate authority should contact.

`--domain` is the zone you add records to, and the one the wildcard
certificate is for: publishing grafana under home.example.com means a
record you create in your own DNS and a certificate for
*.home.example.com. It is deliberately not the resolver's local domain
(`olr dns set --local-domain`), which names the devices in this house.

Usage:
  olr ingress set [flags]

Flags:
      --domain string                         suffix published names live under, e.g. home.example.com
      --email string                          contact address for certificate-expiry warnings
  -h, --help                                  help for set
      --no-raw-caddyfile                      remove the extra Caddyfile configuration
      --provider olr ingress show providers   DNS provider hosting your domain (see olr ingress show providers)
      --raw-caddyfile string                  extra Caddyfile configuration, appended verbatim
      --resolver stringArray                  public resolver for the certificate propagation check, repeatable (default 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8)
      --token string                          provider API credential. Prefer --token-file: a value here is recorded in your shell history
      --token-file string                     read the provider API credential from a file, or from standard input when given -

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
